 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authorization
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request. Missing or invalid credentials return 401 (`unauthorized`). Insufficient permissions return 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+Viewers can use GET routes. Cooks can also post to `/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and `/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers can use every route.
+
+## Routes
+
+`GET /audit` requires a manager key and returns an array of changes newest first. Each entry contains `time`, `keyName`, `method`, `path`, and the HTTP response `status`.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
